From: diogotr7 <diogotr7@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: report at 250 Hz with a finer change threshold

The SET_PAR parameters left the MCU reporting every 9 ms (111 Hz) and only
after a change of 40 counts, about 4% of stick deflection, so small stick
movements were dropped.

Threshold 6 is the floor of the firmware's 7-bit quantisation. The period
byte is value + 2 ms, so 2 gives 4 ms (250 Hz); lower values were
unreliable on the MCU.
---
 drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
index d73c951..d34ba4d 100644
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -241,8 +241,9 @@ static int rsinput_init_commands(struct rsinput_driver *drv) {
     static const uint8_t mcu_params[] = {
         DATA_COMMOD_SET_PAR,
         0x01,
-        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x28,
-        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x07
+        /* threshold 6 = 7-bit quantisation floor; period = value + 2 ms (4 ms = 250 Hz) */
+        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x06,
+        0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x02
     };
     unsigned long timeout = msecs_to_jiffies(MCU_VERSION_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS);
     int attempt;
